      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 4.25,
          "end": 6.13,
          "en": "So let's get started with Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.13,
          "end": 9.16,
          "en": "And what better way to get started than to write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.16,
          "end": 12.76,
          "en": "our first very simple Deno program.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.76,
          "end": 17.193,
          "en": "For that visit deno.land, yes, that is a valid URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 18.11,
          "end": 21.81,
          "en": "And there, you will be able to learn more about Deno,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 21.81,
          "end": 24.02,
          "en": "but you will also learn more about it in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.02,
          "end": 26.64,
          "en": "Of course, most importantly, you will find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.64,
          "end": 29.9,
          "en": "installation instructions for different environments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.9,
          "end": 32.42,
          "en": "and also using different approaches.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.42,
          "end": 35.23,
          "en": "Now you can, of course use any of the approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.23,
          "end": 38.26,
          "en": "being listed here depending on your operating system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.26,
          "end": 39.38,
          "en": "and what you want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.38,
          "end": 42.76,
          "en": "And if you click on this Deno installing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.76,
          "end": 45.54,
          "en": "you also will again find a nice overview",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.54,
          "end": 48.96,
          "en": "of all possible ways of installing Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.96,
          "end": 51.79,
          "en": "Now we might be getting different installation options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.79,
          "end": 53.1,
          "en": "in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.1,
          "end": 56.98,
          "en": "For the moment, I will use one of those options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.98,
          "end": 59.86,
          "en": "On Mac and Linux, you can simply copy this command here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.86,
          "end": 61.79,
          "en": "into the default terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.79,
          "end": 64.62,
          "en": "On Windows you can copy this command here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.62,
          "end": 66.67,
          "en": "into the windows PowerShell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.67,
          "end": 69.03999999999999,
          "en": "So not the normal Command Prompt you got",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.03999999999999,
          "end": 71.68,
          "en": "on your operating system, but the PowerShell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.68,
          "end": 74.01,
          "en": "Which is already pre-installed in which you can launch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.01,
          "end": 76.41,
          "en": "as a program on Windows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.41,
          "end": 78.76,
          "en": "Since I'm on a Mac, I'm going to use this command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.76,
          "end": 81.38,
          "en": "So I'll just paste this here into my terminal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.38,
          "end": 83.33,
          "en": "this curl command and hit Enter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.33,
          "end": 85.52,
          "en": "And this will download this install script,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.52,
          "end": 89.33,
          "en": "download Deno and install Deno on my machine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.33,
          "end": 91.37,
          "en": "Now, what you'll see is that once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.37,
          "end": 94.57,
          "en": "this finishes successfully, that I won't be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.57,
          "end": 95.64,
          "en": "to run Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 95.64,
          "end": 97.75999999999999,
          "en": "Normally there should be a Deno command,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 97.75999999999999,
          "end": 100.32,
          "en": "which you can execute by just typing Deno",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.32,
          "end": 102.61,
          "en": "in your terminal or a Command Prompt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.61,
          "end": 105.313,
          "en": "But if I do that, I get command not found.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 106.17,
          "end": 108.75,
          "en": "But actually I get the fix here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.75,
          "end": 111.6,
          "en": "After the installation, that I should manually add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.6,
          "end": 115.69,
          "en": "the directory to your Home bash profile or similar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 115.69,
          "end": 118.53999999999999,
          "en": "These two entries to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.53999999999999,
          "end": 120.85,
          "en": "You can just copy and paste these entries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 120.85,
          "end": 123.45,
          "en": "And again, depending on the point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 123.45,
          "end": 126.64,
          "en": "you're watching this and on the operating system you're on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 126.64,
          "end": 128.22,
          "en": "the exact instructions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 128.22,
          "end": 130.09,
          "en": "you are seeing here might differ.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 130.09,
          "end": 133.56,
          "en": "Simply follow the instructions you are seeing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 133.56,
          "end": 135.86,
          "en": "In my case, I should add these two instructions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 135.86,
          "end": 138.96,
          "en": "to my bash profile, which is basically a configuration file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 138.96,
          "end": 142.39,
          "en": "for your whole system, which tells your operating system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 142.39,
          "end": 144.89,
          "en": "which commands are available in the Command Prompt,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 144.89,
          "end": 146.22,
          "en": "so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 146.22,
          "end": 148.61,
          "en": "Now, since I'm on Mac OS Catalina,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 148.61,
          "end": 150.66,
          "en": "I don't need the bash profile.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 150.66,
          "end": 153.17000000000002,
          "en": "You only need that if you have a Mac version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 153.17000000000002,
          "end": 156.87,
          "en": "a smaller or older than Catalina.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 156.87,
          "end": 157.742,
          "en": "If you have Catalina,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 157.742,
          "end": 161.61,
          "en": "you should look into your users folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 161.61,
          "end": 165.57,
          "en": "for a .zprofile file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 165.57,
          "end": 166.54,
          "en": "If you're not seeing that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 166.54,
          "end": 168.823,
          "en": "make sure you're showing hidden files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 169.77,
          "end": 172.52,
          "en": "Then you can just edit this and in case you don't have it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 172.52,
          "end": 176.2,
          "en": "you can simply create such a .zprofile file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 176.2,
          "end": 178.173,
          "en": "And I'm going to edit it with TextEdit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 179.28,
          "end": 181.85,
          "en": "And in there, the file might look different for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 181.85,
          "end": 184.9,
          "en": "but in there, the only important thing is that at the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 184.9,
          "end": 188.96,
          "en": "you add these lines you saw in the Command Prompt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 188.96,
          "end": 190.72,
          "en": "So that's what I'm doing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 190.72,
          "end": 194.14,
          "en": "And with that, save that file, close it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 194.14,
          "end": 195.87,
          "en": "and open a new terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 195.87,
          "end": 199.09,
          "en": "So close the terminal and open a new one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 199.09,
          "end": 202.35,
          "en": "And once you do that, you should be able to run Deno",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 202.35,
          "end": 204.29,
          "en": "and it does not give you an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 204.29,
          "end": 207.4,
          "en": "but instead entered this interactive mode here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 207.4,
          "end": 210.1,
          "en": "Now let's explore this and what we can do with Deno",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 210.1,
          "end": 211.203,
          "en": "in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 212.25,
          "end": 215.19,
          "en": "So now this was Mac OS, now for Windows,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 215.19,
          "end": 218.67000000000002,
          "en": "I'm going to grab this command for the PowerShell",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 218.67000000000002,
          "end": 221.01,
          "en": "and just open up the PowerShell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 221.01,
          "end": 224.41,
          "en": "which is a default tool on Windows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 224.41,
          "end": 227.84,
          "en": "And in there, I'll just copy it in and hit Enter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 227.84,
          "end": 230.75,
          "en": "And this is now going to basically send the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 230.75,
          "end": 234.5,
          "en": "to Deno's servers and also run an installation script",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 234.5,
          "end": 237.35,
          "en": "to install Deno on our system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 237.35,
          "end": 240.133,
          "en": "So let's wait for this to finish.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 241.97,
          "end": 245.5,
          "en": "And once this finished, unlike on Mac OS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 245.5,
          "end": 248.86,
          "en": "I'm not even prompted here to do anything else,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 248.86,
          "end": 250.87,
          "en": "and you probably aren't either.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 250.87,
          "end": 252.72,
          "en": "And therefore we can just go ahead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 252.72,
          "end": 256.29,
          "en": "and type the Deno command right away and it should work here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 256.29,
          "end": 258.063,
          "en": "instead of the PowerShell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 259.17,
          "end": 262.61,
          "en": "So that's how easy it is to set up Deno on Windows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 262.61,
          "end": 264.853,
          "en": "And before that also on Mac OS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 266.29,
          "end": 268.93,
          "en": "With that done, you should have Deno installed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 268.93,
          "end": 271.41,
          "en": "and if you now restart the terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 271.41,
          "end": 274.58299999999997,
          "en": "or the Command Prompt or PowerShell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 275.53,
          "end": 278.67,
          "en": "you are able to run Deno just like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 278.67,
          "end": 281.65,
          "en": "This is now a globally available command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 281.65,
          "end": 285.29,
          "en": "And if you run it, you enter the Deno rappel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 285.29,
          "end": 288.08,
          "en": "Now, you know the rappel from Node.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 288.08,
          "end": 291.23,
          "en": "If you run Node, you enter the Node rappel,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 291.23,
          "end": 293.73,
          "en": "and there you can execute basic Node code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 293.73,
          "end": 296.03,
          "en": "You can use it as a basic calculator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 296.03,
          "end": 299.793,
          "en": "and you can quit it with control C or control D.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 301.46,
          "end": 303.51,
          "en": "And for Deno, it's the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 303.51,
          "end": 305.63,
          "en": "You enter the Deno rappel here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 305.63,
          "end": 307.69,
          "en": "You can execute basic Deno code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 307.69,
          "end": 311.09,
          "en": "You can use it as a basic calculator and you can quit it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 311.09,
          "end": 314.313,
          "en": "with control D or by running Close.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 315.16,
          "end": 317.25,
          "en": "Now, the idea is the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 317.25,
          "end": 319.58,
          "en": "This is really just a nice playground,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 319.58,
          "end": 322.36,
          "en": "or to try out some things in reality,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 322.36,
          "end": 325.13,
          "en": "you're going to write JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 325.13,
          "end": 326.93,
          "en": "or TypeScript code with Deno,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 326.93,
          "end": 328.89,
          "en": "and you can then run those code files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 328.89,
          "end": 330.52,
          "en": "with the Deno executable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 330.52,
          "end": 333.09000000000003,
          "en": "That's how you would run most of the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 333.09000000000003,
          "end": 335.07,
          "en": "when working with Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 335.07,
          "end": 336.63,
          "en": "Now, speaking of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 336.63,
          "end": 339.77,
          "en": "let's maybe write some first Deno code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 339.77,
          "end": 342.86,
          "en": "so that we get an idea for how it works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 342.86,
          "end": 346.23,
          "en": "and also so that we can gradually dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 346.23,
          "end": 348.803,
          "en": "into the differences compared to Node.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
